## As built (P13-010 build, 2026-11-09)

- **Layout uses hive labels**, not bare values, so a CHROM dir cannot alias a label dir (CHROM `X` vs
  label `X`). The catalog templates are the contract:
  `out/<vcol>=<v>/variants.pvar` (M), `out/GROUP=<label>/samples.psam` (N),
  `out/<vcol>=<v>/GROUP=<label>/data.pgen` (M·N).
- **CHUNK = `"0"`** per block (one chunk per `<vcol>` value); CHUNK is not in the paths.
- **Reserved names:** `shard_by` GROUP / CHUNK (case-insensitive) is rejected; a `{`/`}` in the
  `shard_by` column name or the target basename is rejected (both are template literals).
- **§6 ATTACH round-trip not asserted for genotypes.** ATTACH's v2 `genotypes` bakes
  `read_pfile([every cell])` with no per-cell `pvar`, so it cannot read this layout (the v2 template
  allows only one shared `.pvar` per variant-block); `genotypes_by_sample` additionally stacks
  sample-blocks. Reader-side follow-on (resolve the templates per cell). The writer is verified by
  `verify_all` + a genotype-orient oracle over all M·N cells.
